{\pntxtb (}{\pntxta )}}{\*\pnseclvl9\pnlcrm\pnstart1\pnindent720\pnhang{\pntxtb (}{\pntxta )}}\pard\plain \qc\nowidctlpar\tx3690\adjustright \fs20\cgrid {\b\f1\fs24\cgrid0 LORDS OF THE REALM 1 }{\f1\fs24\cgrid0 
\par }{\f1\cgrid0 Version 1.04
\par Readme File
\par September 23, 1997
\par }\pard \nowidctlpar\tx3690\adjustright {\f1\cgrid0 
\par ***********************************************************************
\par About This Document:
\par 
\par Thank you for purchasing Lords of the Realm 1
\par 
\par This document contains last-minute information about Lords of the Realm 1 and other information about the program not found in the Help Files.  This README file includes information that 
pertains to general problems and questions you may have concerning this software or your computer. Should you experience any problems with Lords of the Realm 1, please refer to this file for addition help on answering questions about the game and solving 
technical difficulties.
\par 
\par ***********************************************************************
\par 
\par }{\b\f1\fs24\cgrid0 TABLE OF CONTENTS
\par }{\f1\cgrid0 
\par }\pard \nowidctlpar\tx360\tx3690\adjustright {\f1\cgrid0 I.\tab MINIMUM REQUIREMENTS
\par II.\tab GENERAL TECHNICAL ISSUES
\par III.\tab GENERAL GAME ISSUES
\par IV.\tab CONTACTING SIERRA
\par }\pard \nowidctlpar\tx270\tx1710\tx3690\adjustright {\f1\cgrid0 \tab                
\par }\pard \nowidctlpar\tx3690\adjustright {\f1\cgrid0 -----------------------
\par 
\par }{\b\f1\cgrid0 
\par }{\b\f1\fs24\cgrid0 I. MINIMUM REQUIREMENTS
\par }{\f1\cgrid0 
\par 486DX/2-66
\par 8 MB RAM
\par 2X CD-ROM DRIVE
\par LOCAL BUS VIDEO
\par SVGA 640 x 480 x 256 colors
\par 2 MB Hard Disk space
\par Windows compatible sound card
\par Mouse
\par 
\par }{\b\f1\cgrid0 RECOMMENDED REQUIREMENTS
\par 
\par }{\f1\cgrid0 Pentium 75 or better
\par 8 MB RAM
\par 4X CD-ROM Drive 
\par 
\par -----------------------
\par 
\par 
\par }{\b\f1\fs24\cgrid0 II. GENERAL TECHNICAL ISSUES
\par }{\f1\cgrid0 
\par }{\b\f1\cgrid0 INSTALLATION PROCEDURES 
\par 
\par }{\f1\cgrid0 If you are using file deletion tracking utilities such as Mirror, SmartCan, Undelete, etc., please disable these utilities before installing Lords of the Realm 1.
\par 
\par 1) Turn on your computer
\par 2) Wait until the system has come into Windows and has finished loading
\par 3) Open the CD ROM tray door
\par 4) Insert the Lords of the Realm 1  CD ROM
\par 5) Close the door
\par 6) Autoplay should automatically bring up a screen which prompts you to install the game
\par 7) Click on the button that says INSTALL
\par 8) The installation program should guide you through the rest of the process
\par 
\par FYI - If Autoplay is disabled on your computer, 
place the Lords  CD-ROM in the CD-ROM tray and close the door.  Right-click on the CD ROM drive icon inside My Computer (which you may have renamed) and chose "Open".  There will be a number of files and folders visible inside the Lords of the Realm 1  wi
ndows that appears.  Find the icon that is labeled "Setup" and double click on it.  This will launch the Sierra installation program.
\par 
\par 
\par }{\b\f1\cgrid0 WINDOWS PROBLEMS and SOLUTIONS}{\f1\cgrid0 
\par 
\par Windows95 requires some space for virtual memory.  If your hard drive is full, Windows ma
y not have enough room to operate properly.  To check how much hard drive space you have free, double click on "My Computer" on your Desktop and right-click on the drive Windows is running from (usually your C Drive).  Select "Properties" and make sure th
at your Free Space is at least 5,000,000 Bytes (5 MegaBytes).
\par 
\par }{\b\f1\fs24\cgrid0 III. GENERAL GAME ISSUES
\par }\pard\plain \s15\nowidctlpar\widctlpar\tx6750\adjustright \f2\fs20\cgrid {\b\f1 MODEM PLAY NOTE
\par }\pard\plain \nowidctlpar\tx3690\adjustright \fs20\cgrid {\f1 Lords of the Realm 1 was originally written to be a DOS application.  Unfortunately Modem play could not be included in this version of Lords of the Realm 1}{\b\f1\cgrid0 
\par }{\f1\cgrid0 
\par }{\b\f1\cgrid0 MANUAL CORRECTIONS
\par 
\par }{\f1\cgrid0 The hot key for the left mouse button is the F1 Key not the Semi-Colon key as stated in the manual.
\par }{\b\f1\cgrid0 
\par }\pard\plain \s15\nowidctlpar\widctlpar\tx6750\adjustright \f2\fs20\cgrid {\f1\ul An Explanation of Stewardship
\par }{\f1 As explained in the technical supplement, your steward will offer to manage the labor allocations for your fields once  you control three counties.  At the start of each season, he will reallocate the w
orkers you have assigned to grain, sheep, cattle, fields and idle to complete the farming tasks 
\par as best as he can.  He provides a report which indicates which counties require more farmers, and which have too many.
\par 
\par (In addition to this, he now also indicates when the ration  allocations in a county have changed.  This warns you of  food shortages so that you can respond to them.)
\par 
\par It's important to remember that the steward's purpose is NOT to let you ignore your counties while you conquer the enemy  -- h
e will not reclaim fields for you, and you will still  need to manage your castle building and production.  And he  does not act on the warnings he gives you; you must decide on a course of action whenever you have labor excesses, 
\par  abor shortages, or ration changes. 
\par 
\par }{\f1\ul Starting Location
\par }{\f1 Players always start in one of six locations on the map; the  county you start with will have a strong effect on how your  kingdom will progress.  For example, starting in a central  county provides more borders through whic
h you may receive  immigrants (or invaders).  Alternatively, the southwestern- most county gets harsher weather overall than others, and  has only one county for immigrants.
\par 
\par }{\f1\ul Ale Limitations
\par }{\f1 Ale can only be purchased once per county per season.  Its  benefit is also limited to +3 happiness per purchase.  The  Buy Ale panel displays the expected happiness boost for  whatever amount you select.
\par 
\par Ale is consumed immediately upon purchase; as such, it  cannot be transported like other goods.
\par 
\par }{\f1\ul Merchant Delays
\par }{\f1 At harder levels, the appearance of mercenaries may be  delayed.  Expect at least one new merchant to enter the game  each season (until all twelve are present).
\par 
\par }{\f1\ul Castle-Building / Deducting Resources
\par }{\f1 Stone and wood are allocated to castles at the end of a  season (not immediately).  Therefore, if you buy stone or  wood, don't expect to see it deducted (and placed in your  castle) right away.
\par 
\par }{\f1\ul Army Discontent
\par }{\f1 The likelihood of an army to mutiny (i.e. turn into outlaws)  is indicated by a descriptive phrase showing their 
\par discontent.  This phrase appears on the Army panel (when you  click on an army), and on the first screen you see when  starting a siege.
\par 
\par Discontent is based on the army's morale, health, and the  types of units in it.
\par 
\par }{\f1\ul Army Movement Limitations
\par }{\f1 You are not allowed to stand on top of an army or castle  while attacking another army or castle.  Therefore, if you  move to attack an item, and your movement path passes  through another
 obstacle just before reaching that item, the  attack will be disallowed.
\par 
\par }{\f1\ul Mercenary armies
\par }{\f1 Unlike other armies, an army made up only of mercenaries can  disband in any county.
\par 
\par }{\f1\ul Aiming Ladders, Towers and Fighters
\par }{\f1 When sieging, you should always aim a ladder or siege tower  at its target BEFORE you aim infantry at it.
\par 
\par Secondly, you can only aim one fighter-unit at each ladder  or siege tower.
\par 
\par Finally, you can aim ladders and siege towers at structures  of any height; however, they are only effective against the  heights stated in the manual (i.e. any other attacks are  considered "long shots").
\par 
\par }{\f1\ul Picking up Siege Weapons and Fighters
\par }{\f1 If you can't pick up fighters or weapons from the "holding  area" in the top-left corner of the screen, it is because  you have another command currently selected.  Right-click  the mouse to cancel the command.
\par 
\par }{\f1\ul Battering Rams
\par }\pard\plain \s16\sa120\nowidctlpar\widctlpar\adjustright \fs20\cgrid {\f1 Battering rams are only effective at attacking either gatehouses and keeps.
\par }\pard\plain \s15\nowidctlpar\widctlpar\tx6750\adjustright \f2\fs20\cgrid {\f1 
\par }{\f1\ul Eviction and Castles
\par }{\f1 Neutral counties never maintain castles.  Whenever you are  evicted from a county, any castle you have built there will  be demolished.
\par 
\par }{\f1\ul Additional Manual Credits
\par }{\f1 Jeffrey Fiske was not listed in the manual as a Game Tester.
\par }\pard \s15\nowidctlpar\widctlpar\adjustright {\f1 
